# Tests

A behavior change ships with a gdUnit test that fails when the behavior is wrong. Put player tests in `test/player/`.

Before finishing, run the player suite and leave it green:

```
"/Users/bottolo/Applications/Godot.app/Contents/MacOS/Godot" --headless --path . -s res://addons/gdUnit4/bin/GdUnitCmdTool.gd -a res://test/player --ignoreHeadlessMode
```

Run Godot outside the sandbox. The headless editor crashes when it cannot write its log.

Do not delete or weaken a test to make it pass. Fix the behavior, or replace the test when the old behavior was changed on purpose. The new test has to lock in the new behavior.

Docs-only edits do not need a new test.
